// CONFORMANCE: deferred
// Conformance: `catch (e: DbError)` must catch errors classified as
// DbError (or any DbError.* subtype, per the prefix rule in
// `runner::mod.rs::catch_type_matches`).
//
// DEFERRED RATIONALE
// ------------------
// The conformance harness runs without a Postgres connection — the
// integration_db.rs suite owns the testcontainer story. Today the
// runtime classifies an error as `"DbError"` only when the error chain
// either downcasts to `tokio_postgres::Error` (Pass 1) or contains one
// of the substring signatures `deadpool / tokio-postgres / postgres /
// db error / pool / advisory lock / migration / sql` (Pass 2 in
// `classify_jwc_error`).
//
// None of the builtins reachable from .jwc without a DB are reliably
// driven down that path:
//   * `raw_sql` fails with "DATABASE_URL ... is required for db access"
//     when no DB is configured — that string does not contain any of
//     the DbError substring needles.
//   * There is no .jwc surface today for synthesising a typed error
//     ("throw" is not a stable user-facing feature, and the typed
//     `JwcError` enum the docs gesture at is still a follow-up item).
//
// When a follow-up sprint adds either (a) a no-DB classifier hook the
// test can trip, or (b) a userland `throw` form that lets the test
// raise an error whose chain triggers the DbError needle, drop this
// marker and convert it to an active case. The expected stdout below
// reflects the intended behaviour once that path lands.
function main() {
    try {
        // Once unblocked, replace this with a call that classifies as
        // DbError. Today raw_sql with no DATABASE_URL classifies as the
        // generic "Error" supertype, which is why the test is deferred.
        let _ignored = raw_sql("select 1");
        print("never");
    } catch (e: DbError) {
        print("caught db error");
    }
}
